.KEY TO/A,ALL/S
.BRA {
.KET }
; Get-UP-Term: the bootstrap kit (owner 2026-11-12). Fetches the UP-Term base kit (up-term.lha) from the
; release feed over https into the TO drawer, unpacks it there (drawer up-term in TO) and runs the kit's own
; install.dos. install.dos asks its questions and installs UP-Term to its own default drawer, SYS:UP-Term,
; not to TO. ALL then installs every package of the feed through upkg.
;   CD <this drawer>
;   Execute Get-UP-Term TO <drawer with about 110 MB free for the archive and the unpacked kit, e.g. Work:> [ALL]
; Needs: lha in the path, a 68020 or better. A TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library) is needed for the download;
; when the Amiga has none, the kit installs one first (below).
; No TCP/IP stack: the evidence of P_TCPCHECK (dist/common/tcpstack.installer), in this order: tcpprobe (opens
; bsdsocket.library, returns 0 when it opens: a running stack or the emulator's own), the assigns AmiNetXDuo:,
; AmiTCP:, Miami:, Genesis:, TheWire:, then S:AmiNetXDuo-Files, LIBS:genesis.library, LIBS:bsdsocket.library on disk.
; None of them: the script runs AmiNetXDuo 1.0.0-rc2's own Install-AmiNetXDuo (MIT, the drawer AmiNetXDuo here, as
; the full kit's P_ANX does: a CD into the drawer, then its Installer script; it asks for the network card's
; SANA-II driver and for DHCP or a fixed address), then asks for a reboot and quits; run it again after the reboot.
; Return codes: 0 UP-Term installed; 5 AmiNetXDuo was installed now, reboot and run Get-UP-Term again (nothing
; was fetched); 20 failed (a message says which step; nothing of UP-Term was installed).
; The download is certificate-checked: when the system holds no root certificates for bebboget yet
; (ENVARC:certs), installcerts writes the ones of cacert.pem (Mozilla's list, from curl.se) there first.
; bebboget and installcerts are Stefan Franke's bebboget 1.11, GPL v3+ (COPYING, SOURCE.txt; bebboget
; is a modified build, its change is bebboget-up-term.diff; the source archive is in up-term.lha, published at
; the same place: Files/net/bebboget-1.11).
FailAt 21
Which >NIL: lha
If WARN
  Echo "Get-UP-Term: lha is not in the path (Aminet util/arc/lha.run). Nothing was changed."
  Quit 20
EndIf
If NOT EXISTS "{TO}"
  Echo "Get-UP-Term: {TO} does not exist. Nothing was changed."
  Quit 20
EndIf
Set UPTSTACK no
tcpprobe >NIL:
If NOT WARN
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
Assign >NIL: EXISTS AmiNetXDuo:
If NOT WARN
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
Assign >NIL: EXISTS AmiTCP:
If NOT WARN
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
Assign >NIL: EXISTS Miami:
If NOT WARN
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
Assign >NIL: EXISTS Genesis:
If NOT WARN
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
Assign >NIL: EXISTS TheWire:
If NOT WARN
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
If EXISTS S:AmiNetXDuo-Files
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
If EXISTS LIBS:genesis.library
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
If EXISTS LIBS:bsdsocket.library
  Set UPTSTACK yes
EndIf
If $UPTSTACK EQ no
  UnSet UPTSTACK
  If NOT EXISTS AmiNetXDuo/Install-AmiNetXDuo
    Echo "Get-UP-Term: this Amiga has no TCP/IP stack and the drawer AmiNetXDuo is missing here. Nothing was changed."
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  If NOT EXISTS AmiNetXDuo/Installer
    Which >NIL: Installer
    If WARN
      Echo "Get-UP-Term: this Amiga has no TCP/IP stack and no Installer program to install one. Nothing was changed."
      Quit 20
    EndIf
  EndIf
  Echo "This Amiga has no TCP/IP stack (no bsdsocket.library), and the download needs one."
  Echo "Starting the AmiNetXDuo installer (a free TCP/IP stack): it asks for your network card's"
  Echo "SANA-II driver and for DHCP or a fixed address. UP-Term itself is not installed yet."
  CD AmiNetXDuo
  Installer SCRIPT Install-AmiNetXDuo APPNAME AmiNetXDuo MINUSER AVERAGE DEFUSER AVERAGE NOLOG
  CD /
  If NOT EXISTS S:AmiNetXDuo-Files
    Echo "Get-UP-Term: AmiNetXDuo was not installed, so there is still no TCP/IP stack."
    Echo "Run Execute Get-UP-Term TO {TO} again to retry, or install another TCP/IP stack."
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo "AmiNetXDuo is installed. Reboot the Amiga so that it starts, then run"
  Echo "Execute Get-UP-Term TO {TO} again in this drawer to fetch and install UP-Term."
  Quit 5
EndIf
UnSet UPTSTACK
If NOT EXISTS ENVARC:certs
  Echo "Installing the root certificates (ENVARC:certs) ..."
  installcerts cacert.pem
  If WARN
    Echo "Get-UP-Term: installcerts failed."
    Quit 20
  EndIf
EndIf
Echo "Fetching up-term.lha (about 33 MB) into {TO} ..."
Assign UPTGET: "{TO}"
; bebboget (UP-Term's build, bebboget-up-term.diff) returns 10 on a failed connection, a failed certificate
; check or an HTTP error status (4xx/5xx). An old archive goes first, and lha tests the new one as well, so a
; cut-off file is not unpacked either.
Delete >NIL: UPTGET:up-term.lha
bebboget -O -D "{TO}" -o up-term.lha @FEED@/up-term.lha
If WARN
  Delete >NIL: UPTGET:up-term.lha
  Assign UPTGET: REMOVE
  Echo "Get-UP-Term: the download failed (is the TCP/IP stack running?)."
  Quit 20
EndIf
lha >NIL: -q t UPTGET:up-term.lha
If WARN
  Delete >NIL: UPTGET:up-term.lha
  Assign UPTGET: REMOVE
  Echo "Get-UP-Term: the downloaded up-term.lha is damaged."
  Quit 20
EndIf
Echo "Unpacking up-term.lha into the drawer up-term in {TO} ..."
lha -q x UPTGET:up-term.lha UPTGET:
If WARN
  Assign UPTGET: REMOVE
  Echo "Get-UP-Term: lha could not unpack {TO} up-term.lha."
  Quit 20
EndIf
Delete >NIL: UPTGET:up-term.lha
Echo "Starting the kit's install.dos: it asks its questions and installs UP-Term to SYS:UP-Term (not to {TO})."
Execute UPTGET:up-term/Files/install.dos UPTGET:up-term/Files
If WARN
  Assign UPTGET: REMOVE
  Echo "Get-UP-Term: the install did not finish; the kit is in {TO} up-term."
  Quit 20
EndIf
Assign UPTGET: REMOVE
If "{ALL}" EQ "ALL"
  Stack 262144
  UP-Term:bin/upkg update
  UP-Term:bin/upkg install --all
EndIf
